Z||000000||sailordude||12-04-2001||03:19 PM||||Hey guys,<BR>I'm not interested in buying one today, or even this month, but one day (when I'm not broke) I would like to find me a Supercharged 3800 engine to put in my sweet 1985 GT.  So I was wondering where I should start looking?  Any ideas guys? I mean where did everyone find these sweet motors? Did they just go to the wreckers and trip over them one day?  Well any ideas forward them my way.  Thanks again.<P>Laters,<P>Darren||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||12-04-2001||05:57 PM||||Basically start combing junk yards!  Preferably locate a Bonneville SSEi (the newer the better) or anything similiar.  You'll probably want to be sure to get a 3800 Series II supercharged (more power/better overall engine than the series I).  You can also watch Ebay or your local "trader" magazines for used/rebuilt engines.<P>There are a handful of places that sell GM test engines as well:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.cs-performance.com/3800/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cs-performance.com/3800/index.html</A> <P>Good luck!<P>Oh yeah, BTW- if you run across a good condition 3800 SII "just the Supercharger" for a really good deal... let me know  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||hugh||12-04-2001||06:46 PM||||Caspers in Mundelien(sp),Illinois has superchargers that are new and also heat tested(I think).Check them out.John Spina at Caspers is a first class guy.||||reg||14
